WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:06.886
Now, reader, the princess loved the lake with all her heart.

2
00:00:06.887 --> 00:00:11.320
She knew where to find its best diving spots.

3
00:00:11.321 --> 00:00:15.952
She knew where its tallest banks sat.

4
00:00:15.953 --> 00:00:24.598
She knew where all its fish and wild creatures lived.

5
00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:29.498
So, of course, Ellen knew at once that the lake was changing.

6
00:00:29.499 --> 00:00:34.107
She first noticed it while swimming with the prince.

7
00:00:34.108 --> 00:00:38.057
She shot to the surface and looked around.

8
00:00:38.058 --> 00:00:41.084
"Something's wrong with the lake!"

9
00:00:41.085 --> 00:00:47.190
The prince popped up nearby. "It looks fine to me."

10
00:00:47.191 --> 00:00:50.349
"No, the lake is different!"

11
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:55.253
She took off, swimming toward a deeper part of the lake. He

12
00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:58.197
swam after her, wondering if she was sick. "Ellen!

13
00:00:58.198 --> 00:01:00.837
Are you okay?" Ellen

14
00:01:00.838 --> 00:01:04.511
didn't reply or look back. Instead

15
00:01:04.512 --> 00:01:17.695
she darted from place to place, checking different spots around the lake. The

16
00:01:17.696 --> 00:01:22.297
next day when they met, she was even more upset. "The

17
00:01:22.298 --> 00:01:30.637
banks are too dry. The grass and plants are dying." She

18
00:01:30.638 --> 00:01:34.113
pointed to rocks baking in the sun. "Look!

19
00:01:34.114 --> 00:01:39.366
Those rocks are usually under the water." The

20
00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:42.694
confused prince tried to comfort her. But

21
00:01:42.695 --> 00:01:47.171
she pushed him away. "This

22
00:01:47.172 --> 00:01:49.779
is terrible," she cried. "The

23
00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:58.370
lake is losing its water!" ***

24
00:01:58.371 --> 00:02:11.480
Agnes stayed in the cellar for seven days and seven nights.

25
00:02:11.481 --> 00:02:14.865
Finally the water dragon dropped onto the floor.

26
00:02:14.866 --> 00:02:21.073
It quickly dried up and turned back to seaweed.

27
00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:27.698
The witch grabbed the seaweed and looked up.

28
00:02:27.699 --> 00:02:33.566
Water was beginning to drip from the stone.

29
00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:36.938
"The spell worked!" she cried.

30
00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:41.304
Soon lake water would be rushing into her cellars.

31
00:02:41.305 --> 00:02:47.058
She had to get back upstairs—fast!

32
00:02:47.059 --> 00:02:50.210
*** The next day Agnes checked the

33
00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:52.707
lake. Most of its water was gone.

34
00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:56.404
But here and there were a few shallow pools.

35
00:02:56.405 --> 00:03:03.491
Agnes frowned. "The spell is taking too long!"

36
00:03:03.492 --> 00:03:07.402
That night Agnes went back to the lake.

37
00:03:07.403 --> 00:03:15.609
She walked all around, sprinkling her potion everywhere.

38
00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:27.688
She even tossed some into the air, at the princess' window.

39
00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:32.825
An instant later the kingdom's rivers and brooks stopped flowing.

40
00:03:32.826 --> 00:03:36.492
Water no longer rushed down its mountains.

41
00:03:36.493 --> 00:03:39.489
Fountains and wells went dry.

42
00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.571
Even babies' tears dried up.

43
00:03:42.572 --> 00:03:47.517
At the lake the last bit of water was finally gone.

